WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.793
Secure Express applications depend on
routing, middleware, code,

2
00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:13.055
configuration, dependencies, runtime
context, and operations.

3
00:00:13.135 --> 00:00:18.214
Treat middleware order as
security-relevant design.

4
00:00:18.294 --> 00:00:25.028
Separate public, authenticated,
privileged, service-only, webhook,

5
00:00:25.108 --> 00:00:27.758
and administrative routes.

6
00:00:27.838 --> 00:00:33.247
Enforce authentication and authorization
server-side.

7
00:00:33.327 --> 00:00:36.970
Validate request data before using it.

8
00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:42.460
Shape responses intentionally and handle
errors safely.

9
00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:47.398
Protect cookies, sessions, CSRF-sensitive
flows,

10
00:00:47.478 --> 00:00:54.102
and CORS configuration based on the real
browser and deployment model.

11
00:00:54.182 --> 00:00:59.039
Production readiness matters as much as
route code.

12
00:00:59.119 --> 00:01:05.964
Apply security headers thoughtfully,
review TLS and proxy assumptions,

13
00:01:06.044 --> 00:01:10.460
remove development behavior from
production,

14
00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:15.618
manage dependencies deliberately, protect
secrets,

15
00:01:15.698 --> 00:01:23.758
separate environment configuration, and
avoid leaking sensitive values into logs or

16
00:01:23.838 --> 00:01:24.610
images.

17
00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:28.775
Add abuse controls, safe logs, monitoring,

18
00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:36.694
and operational ownership so the team can
see whether the application is behaving as

19
00:01:36.774 --> 00:01:37.767
expected.

20
00:01:37.847 --> 00:01:43.919
A practical first week plan can produce
meaningful improvement.

21
00:01:43.999 --> 00:01:48.415
Map routes and middleware in the order
they run.

22
00:01:48.495 --> 00:01:54.457
Identify unprotected or inconsistently
protected endpoints.

23
00:01:54.537 --> 00:02:01.713
Review authentication and object-level
access checks on high-risk routes.

24
00:02:01.793 --> 00:02:06.871
Add schema validation and allowlisted
update fields.

25
00:02:06.951 --> 00:02:09.932
Check cookie and CORS settings.

26
00:02:10.012 --> 00:02:14.428
Review secrets and production error
handling.

27
00:02:14.508 --> 00:02:17.820
Add rate limits to sensitive flows.

28
00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:25.297
Improve security logging so incident
response starts with evidence instead of

29
00:02:25.377 --> 00:02:26.260
guesses.
